# QODIQA Backup Scheduling — systemd EnvironmentFile template.
#
# Copy to /etc/qodiqa/backup.env (mode 0640, owned by root:qodiqa) and fill
# in real values. This is the self-hosted/systemd-timer equivalent of
# deploy/kubernetes/base/backup-configmap.yaml + base/secret.yaml's backup-related
# keys — every value here is read by the SAME scripts
# (scripts/pg-backup.sh, scripts/dr/*.js), so behavior is identical to the
# Kubernetes CronJob form.
#
# Consumed by: deploy/systemd/qodiqa-pg-backup-*.service,
#              deploy/systemd/qodiqa-dr-backup.service,
#              deploy/systemd/qodiqa-dr-restore-validation.service

# ── PostgreSQL connection (libpq standard env vars) ──────────────────────────
PGHOST=localhost
PGPORT=5432
PGDATABASE=qodiqa
# backups connect as the dedicated read-only backup role (migration 067:
# BYPASSRLS + SELECT only). As qodiqa_app, pg_dump failed every full backup and the DR JSON dump
# silently dropped every tenant-scoped row. Rotate the role's password and put it here.
PGUSER=qodiqa_backup
PGPASSWORD=<REPLACE_WITH_POSTGRES_BACKUP_PASSWORD>
# never fall back to a plaintext connection (libpq's default is `prefer`). A
# production gateway only boots with PostgreSQL TLS, so the server already serves it. Better still, verify the server
# certificate: PGSSLMODE=verify-full plus PGSSLROOTCERT=<path to the CA that issued it>.
PGSSLMODE=require

# ── scripts/pg-backup.sh ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
QODIQA_BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/qodiqa
QODIQA_BACKUP_RETAIN_DAYS=30
QODIQA_BACKUP_RETAIN_DAILY=7
QODIQA_BACKUP_RETAIN_WEEKLY=4
QODIQA_BACKUP_RETAIN_MONTHLY=12
QODIQA_BACKUP_JOBS=4
QODIQA_BACKUP_HMAC_KEY=<REPLACE_WITH_32+_CHAR_SECRET_openssl_rand_hex_32>
# encryption at rest — a DIFFERENT 32+ char secret; keep a copy off this host (no key, no restore).
QODIQA_BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<REPLACE_WITH_32+_CHAR_SECRET_openssl_rand_hex_32>
QODIQA_BACKUP_REQUIRE_ENCRYPTION=true
# Optional: a command run as `<cmd> <backup file> <seal file>` after each backup, to copy both off-site.
#QODIQA_BACKUP_OFFSITE_COMMAND=/usr/local/bin/qodiqa-offsite-copy
QODIQA_BACKUP_METRICS_FILE=/var/backups/qodiqa/metrics/qodiqa_pg_backup.prom

# ── scripts/dr/backup.js + retention.js + verify.js + cycle.js ──────────────
# NOTE: QODIQA_BACKUP_METRICS_FILE is set ABOVE for scripts/pg-backup.sh.
# The DR services (qodiqa-dr-backup.service, qodiqa-dr-restore-validation.
# service) need a DIFFERENT value for the same var name, so — since a flat
# EnvironmentFile can only define a key once — they override it directly in
# their own unit file's `Environment=` line (which takes precedence over
# this file), rather than a second definition here that would silently
# shadow the one above.
QODIQA_DR_BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/qodiqa-dr
QODIQA_DR_RETAIN_DAILY=7
QODIQA_DR_RETAIN_WEEKLY=4
QODIQA_DR_RETAIN_MONTHLY=12

# Point these at the SAME paths the live qodiqa.service uses (self-hosted
# single-instance deployments run on the same host, so every file-based
# component is reachable — see qodiqa-dr-backup.service's header comment).
QODIQA_AUDIT_LOG=/opt/qodiqa/logs/audit.log
QODIQA_KEYS_PATH=/opt/qodiqa/data/keys.json
QODIQA_KEYS_ARCHIVE_PATH=/opt/qodiqa/data/key-archive.json
#/INJ-3/#283: renamed from QODIQA_POLICY_STORE_PATH — that variable
# belonged to a dead module (policy/policyStore.js) that has been removed.
# QODIQA_POLICY_STORE is what the live policy store (src/core/policy/store.js)
# actually reads. If this deployment previously set QODIQA_POLICY_STORE_PATH,
# update it to QODIQA_POLICY_STORE or DR backup/restore will silently operate
# on a file the running server never reads from.
QODIQA_POLICY_STORE=/opt/qodiqa/config/policy-store.json
# the rest of the recovery-critical file state, at the live service's paths. NODE_ENV=production
# makes the DR backup resolve the production control plane (PostgreSQL: RBAC, signing identities, tenants, policies —
# the backup then refuses to run without --with-postgres) and refuse to run when the anchor export / local witness log
# paths are not set, instead of silently leaving them out. The database part is a pg_dump (custom format) of a snapshot
# taken before the files are copied, made with the libpq PG* variables above (no QODIQA_PG_URL needed); pg_dump's major
# must equal the server's (scripts/dr/pgDump.js refuses otherwise) — install the matching postgresql-client.
# For full certificate verification set PGSSLMODE=verify-full and PGSSLROOTCERT=<the CA that issued the server cert>.
# The witness KEY and its public-key trust set are NOT backed up (deployment configuration, restored from the secret
# store with the KEK) — docs/operations/restore-runbook.md §3A.
NODE_ENV=production
QODIQA_TRANSPARENCY_KEYS_PATH=/opt/qodiqa/data/transparency-keys.json
QODIQA_MAC_KEYS_PATH=/opt/qodiqa/data/mac-keys.json
QODIQA_PRQ_JOURNAL_DIR=/opt/qodiqa/data/prq-journal
QODIQA_WITNESS_MODE=local
QODIQA_WITNESS_LOG_PATH=/opt/qodiqa/anchors/witness-log.jsonl
QODIQA_ANCHOR_EXPORT_PATH=/opt/qodiqa/anchors/anchors.jsonl
# Pilot: backups are OFF-PEAK (a hot real-size backup raised segment p95 to 563-949 ms). Set the agreed window with no
# contracted traffic; dr/backup.js and pg-backup.sh full|incremental then refuse to start outside it (loudly). Schedule
# the timers inside it (restore-runbook.md §3A.2). Unset = unrestricted.
#QODIQA_BACKUP_WINDOW_UTC=02:00-05:00

# ── scripts/backup-audit-log.sh ───────────────────────────
# Consumed by qodiqa-audit-log-backup.service / qodiqa-audit-log-backup-verify.service,
# both firing every 5 minutes and
# disaster-recovery.md §1 for the RPO this makes true.
QODIQA_AUDIT_BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/qodiqa/audit
QODIQA_AUDIT_BACKUP_RETAIN_DAYS=90
QODIQA_AUDIT_BACKUP_MAX_AGE_SECONDS=600
QODIQA_AUDIT_BACKUP_METRICS_FILE=/var/backups/qodiqa/audit/metrics/qodiqa_audit_log_backup.prom

# ── scripts/pg-wal-archive.sh ──
# archive_command target; see docs/operations/backup-runbook.md's WAL
# archiving prerequisites block for the required postgresql.conf settings.
QODIQA_WAL_ARCHIVE_DIR=/var/backups/qodiqa/wal-archive
QODIQA_WAL_ARCHIVE_RETAIN_DAYS=7
QODIQA_WAL_ARCHIVE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300
QODIQA_WAL_ARCHIVE_MAX_AGE_SECONDS=600

# Isolated restore-validation target — MUST be a genuinely separate database
# from PGDATABASE above (see qodiqa-dr-restore-validation.service). Create it
# once and apply migrations exactly as
# .github/workflows/backup-restore.yml's dr-postgres job does:
#   createdb -h $PGHOST -U <an admin/owner identity> qodiqa_restore_validation
#   (not $PGUSER: that is the read-only qodiqa_backup role, which can neither create a
#   database nor write the restore target — QODIQA_PG_RESTORE_URL below keeps its own writer identity)
#   QODIQA_PG_URL=postgresql://... node src/infra/postgres/migrate.js
# verify-full = what node-postgres already does for `require` today, spelled out so its next major (which
# gives `require` the weaker libpq meaning) cannot silently drop certificate verification.
QODIQA_PG_RESTORE_URL=postgresql://qodiqa_app:<PASSWORD>@localhost:5432/qodiqa_restore_validation?sslmode=verify-full

# ── Alerting (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Slack/PagerDuty-compatible webhook. Treat this file's permissions as
# sensitive once this is filled in — most webhook URLs embed a bearer-token-
# like path segment. Leave unset to disable alerting (all scripts no-op safely).
# ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/REPLACE/WITH/REAL
